# [WEBBOTAUTH](../wg/webbotauth.html)

## Summary

The WEBBOTAUTH working group met at IETF 127 to review progress on its adopted document, [`draft-ietf-webbotauth-httpsig-protocol`](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-webbotauth-httpsig-protocol/), examine implementer feedback, and evaluate several non-adopted proposals. Key technical topics included refining HTTP message signature parameters, establishing minimal signature component baselines, standardizing error reporting, and addressing ecosystem centralization risks for independent crawlers. The working group also held extensive scope discussions around proposals for IP range discovery, granular sub-agent metadata, and privacy-preserving rate limiting, confirming that tracking or assigning reputation to individual users or sub-agent sessions remains out of scope under the current charter.

